# The build context is packages/basecamp. Everything the image needs is copied
# explicitly by deploy/Dockerfile; this keeps the rest out of the context, which
# is both a speed question and a correctness one — a stray node_modules or a
# live database file in the context ends up in the image.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# The live databases and the audit trail. Copying a development database into
# an image is how a container comes up holding somebody's laptop data.
#
# `**`, not `db/*.db`: a plain `*` does not cross a separator, so `db/*.db`
# excluded `db/basecamp.db` and copied `db/db/basecamp.db` — and `db/db/` is
# exactly what a relative `database { path }` resolved against the wrong working
# directory creates (FJS-449). It is git-ignored, so it appears in no diff.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
db/audit

# Built output — the image builds its own, from the source it copied, so a
# stale dist on the host cannot become the thing that ships.
web/dist

# The generated build inputs are copied by an explicit COPY and must NOT be
# excluded; everything else under deploy/ is host-side tooling.
deploy/build.mjs
deploy/docker-compose.yml

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
